            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Invention of TCP/IP</strong><br>\nIn the early 1970s, Robert Kahn collaborated with Vinton Cerf to create the Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) and the Internet Protocol (IP), commonly referred to as TCP/IP. This protocol suite became the foundation for data exchange on the internet. Their work allowed different kinds of networks to interconnect and communicate, which was a revolutionary step in the creation of a global network.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact of TCP/IP</strong><br>\nThe implementation of TCP/IP had a profound impact on the way information is shared and accessed. It provided a standardized method for different computer networks to communicate, paving the way for the modern internet's expansive growth. Kahn's vision and technical expertise were crucial in developing a protocol that could scale with the increasing number of users and data traffic.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Career and Recognition</strong><br>\nRobert Kahn continued his career in networking and technology, contributing to various projects and steering the course of internet development. For his work on TCP/IP, he received numerous awards and honors, including the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2005. His contributions are recognized globally, and he is regarded as one of the pioneers of the internet.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
