          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Corporation for National Research Initiatives (CNRI)</strong><br>\nIn 1986, Kahn founded the Corporation for National Research Initiatives (CNRI), a non-profit organization dedicated to fostering research for the national interest. At CNRI, he worked on digital object architecture, which is vital for managing information in a networked environment. His ongoing work at CNRI aims to enhance the internet's functionality and efficiency.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on Digital Communication</strong><br>\nKahn's work has greatly influenced the way digital communication systems are designed and operated today. He has been a proponent of network system development that emphasizes openness, scalability, and interoperability. His contributions have helped shape the internet into a robust platform for innovation and communication.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Future of Networking</strong><br>\nThe legacy of Robert Kahn is firmly embedded in the history of the internet and the development of computer networking. He continues to work on advancing internet technology and advocating for responsible innovation. His foresight into the needs of a changing digital landscape ensures that his work remains relevant as the internet evolves into the future.</p>\n"
              },
